================================================================================
3. COMMERCIAL & CORPORATE LICENSE (5% PROFIT SHARE)
================================================================================

Licensor hereby grants to any Commercial Entity a worldwide, non-exclusive
license to use, modify, embed, host (including closed-source products, SaaS,
APIs, and embedded/edge hardware), and commercially distribute the Covered Work,
strictly conditioned upon full compliance with ALL of the following terms:

  (a) Five Percent (5%) Profit Share: The Commercial Entity shall pay to
      Licensor five percent (5%) of all Attributable Net Profit generated from
      any commercial product, hosted service, API, hardware device, or
      for-profit deployment utilizing the Covered Work (or models trained,
      quantized, compressed, or modified using the Covered Work).

  (b) Notification & Quarterly Accounting: Within thirty (30) days of first
      commercial deployment or first commercial revenue (whichever occurs
      earlier), the Commercial Entity must notify Licensor via GitHub
      (https://github.com/batteryphil) by opening a "[Commercial 5% License
      Registration]" notice or executing a direct payment schedule with
      Licensor. Profit-share statements and payments shall be remitted within
      thirty (30) days following the close of each calendar quarter in which
      Attributable Net Profit exceeds USD $1,000.

  (c) Internal Non-Revenue R&D Evaluation Grace Period: A Commercial Entity may
      internally evaluate and benchmark the Covered Work for up to sixty (60)
      days prior to production or commercial deployment without fee.

  (d) Optional Flat-Fee Enterprise Buyout: Commercial Entities preferring a
      fixed annual or perpetual flat-fee buyout in lieu of the 5% profit share
      may negotiate a separate written Enterprise License Agreement directly
      with Philip Bartsch (@batteryphil).

  (e) Automatic Termination on Breach: Any commercial use by a Commercial Entity
      that fails to honor Section 3(a)-(b) automatically terminates all rights
      granted under this Section 3 until cured in writing with Licensor.

